<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices mixed on limited arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices mixed on limited arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices were steady in domestic markets on Wednesday but plant delivery rates fell by 100 rupees per tonne, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said arrivals were limited.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were steady in thin trading.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices firmed on good export demand. Soymeal yellow was $295-296 per tonne for current season's September-October delivery and was $279-280 for new season's November, December and January shipment. Rapeseed extraction was $129-130 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,450 rupees FOR (Free on Rail) Bedibunder and was 4,450 rupees FOR (Free on Rail) Bhavnagar port.</p>
